kv, kv-v2 
kv-v2 Concepts:-
The data/ and metadata/ prefix is required for API and when writing Vault policies and not whe using CLI
vault kv put kv/app/db pass=123 user=admin group=abc  (same syntax for both kv and kv-v2)
If the latest version of the secret has been deleted (KV V2), it will return the related metadata but no data (secrets)

DB secret engine:-
generates dynamic credentials (username and password). Creds generated based on roles (based on permissions required) and lease is attached to creds.
You can easily rotate the root credentials for each database configuration using the rotate-root endpoint. It ensures that only Vault and the Database server know the root
credentials – no human would know the creds.
Static role is a 1-1 mapping of a role to an existing, static user on the database. Vault will rotate the credential based on a configurable time period but
the user does not change
vault read database/creds/app-hcvop
Like anything else in Vault, a Vault client requires a token with a policy that has permission to generate database credentials. # Get credentials from the database secrets engine
path "database/creds/app-hcvop" {
capabilities = ["read"]
}
